00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:45,030
Oh, welcome back, you're quite late.

822
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:47,260
How was school?

823
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:48,390
Hm?

824
00:06:48,390 --> 00:06:50,680
It was okay.

825
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:54,270
Oh, right! I happened to run 
into his mom at the supermarket.

826
00:06:54,270 --> 00:06:57,300
She said she still works 
at the municipal hospital over there.

827
00:06:57,550 --> 00:06:59,770
I mean, Haruto-kun's mom... Haruto-kun's!

828
00:06:59,770 --> 00:07:03,860
I'm gonna hang out with Haruto tomorrow, 
so I might not be able to clean my room up much.

829
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:06,200
What? I can't hear you!

830
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:08,600
I'm kinda tired.

831
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,330
Natsume sure has changed.

832
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:21,920
I screwed up... I'm so freakin' lame.

833
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,460
I'm home!

834
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,420
Welcome back!

835
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,950
You got home late today. Did you eat dinner?

836
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:29,470
Do we have anything?

837
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:33,640
I ate with Haru-chan. We have leftovers 
in the pot, so I'll warm it up for you.

838
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,100
Oh, I can do that!

839
00:07:39,730 --> 00:07:43,230
Well, I can just tell Morikawa tomorrow, right?

840
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:46,320
Onee-chan, let me borrow your coat tomorrow.

841
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:47,860
My coat?

842
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:51,080
<i>Shark Skin Squadron! Sharkman is here!</i>

843
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:51,080
<i>Shark Skin Squadron! Sharkman is here!</i>

844
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,410
Whale Shark Vacuum!

845
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:54,400
Hammerhead Shark Hammerhead!

846
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:58,460
My friends and I are having a celebration party, 
so I wanna wear your coat to it.

847
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:02,090
Oh, sorry. I'm going out tomorrow.

848
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:04,960
What?! But you said you didn't have any plans!

849
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,050
Sorry.

850
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,470
Where are you going?

851
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:09,760
To the aquarium.

852
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,970
With whom?

853
00:08:10,970 --> 00:08:14,600
With Yoriko and some friends from class, I guess?

854
00:08:15,310 --> 00:08:16,890
Why do you sound so unsure?

855
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:20,370
Well, I've only really talked to Yoriko about it.

856
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:25,110
But after I'd said I had nothing to do, I thought 
that turning down the invitation would be weird, too.

857
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:26,270
Are you going with a boy?

858
00:08:27,490 --> 00:08:28,650
Yeah.

859
00:08:28,650 --> 00:08:30,030
Then, it's a date!

860
00:08:30,530 --> 00:08:32,030
I don't think so.

861
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:34,160
It's definitely a date!

862
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:35,880
It's almost Christmas!

863
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:38,020
It's the eve of Christmas Eve, you know!

864
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:42,750
If that were the case, I think he would've 
invited some other girls from class, not me.

865
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:45,710
Oh, and after you finish that, go take a bath.

866
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,920
I'm jealous!

867
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:49,680
The aquarium sounds nice!

868
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,180
Uh-huh, uh-huh!

869
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,180
The aquarium sounds nice!

870
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:57,520
<i>I'm so very jealous! The aquarium sounds nice!</i>

871
00:09:03,770 --> 00:09:06,650
I wonder why he came back now...

872
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:14,910
Izumi remembers that, doesn't he?

873
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:20,000
After I had forgotten all about it...

874
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,800
I'm heading out!

875
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,210
Have a nice day!

876
00:09:31,430 --> 00:09:33,600
Because I'm not going to clean up.

877
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:42,770
Shouldn't you quit while you're ahead?

878
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:43,560
Hm?

879
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:51,450
So, today...

880
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:54,280
Would it be better if I couldn't come 
'cause something suddenly came up?

881
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:58,740
You can come as you normally would. 
We'd get nervous if it was suddenly just the two of us.

882
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:02,000
Oh, awesome! Yay!

883
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:04,790
Ow...!

884
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:07,920
Your muscles hurt? Are you a geezer?

885
00:10:11,170 --> 00:10:12,590
Was her name Morikawa-san?

886
00:10:12,590 --> 00:10:14,300
Hm? Yeah...

887
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:16,050
Why Morikawa-san?

888
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,930
Does it matter?

889
00:10:21,390 --> 00:10:26,370
She's in the Band Club, and she'd come 
to cheer us on every year at the summer tournament,

890
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:28,690
even in the sweltering heat.

891
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:33,070
That's tougher than what we 
baseball players have to deal with.

892
00:10:33,070 --> 00:10:36,240
Maybe. So, is that all?

893
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:39,880
After I saw her playing the trumpet,
I couldn't get her out of my mind...

894
00:10:40,790 --> 00:10:44,850
And before I knew it, I couldn't help looking 
at Morikawa the entire time.

895
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:48,920
You have to focus on the game 
when you're playing on the field.

896
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:49,960
Shut up.

897
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:53,800
Anyway, I couldn't get her out of my mind, 
so what else can I say?

898
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:57,720
I don't know what to say to such an honest confession...

899
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,720
I'd be able to say it, if it were to you.

900
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,840
Hey, Eita, did you get a girlfriend 
before you transferred?

901
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,820
That's a super annoying question.

902
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:12,990
You don't got one? Then, 
everything's turned out all right!

903
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:13,740
What?

904
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:15,780
You used to like Natsume, right?

905
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:18,280
What leads you to say that?

906
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:20,700
You told me in middle school.

907
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:21,880
No, I didn't!

908
00:11:22,330 --> 00:11:24,080
Then, how do I know that?

909
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:26,710
That's what I'd like to know.

910
00:11:26,710 --> 00:11:29,710
Huh. Well, I'll support you.

911
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,590
That's all in the past...

912
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:36,680
You guys sure got here early.

913
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,680
Eita and I had a lot of catching up to do. Right?

914
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,640
I guess.

915
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,270
What did you guys talk about?

916
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:46,690
Stuff from the past.

917
00:11:46,690 --> 00:11:48,060
I see...

918
00:11:49,190 --> 00:11:50,810
Oh, they're already here.

919
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,610
Live Sharksucker Missile!

920
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:58,950
B-B-Boom! Boom!

921
00:11:58,950 --> 00:12:02,370
Sorry, they said they wanted to come 
to the aquarium, no matter what.

922
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:03,870
All right! This is the final blow!

923
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:04,620
Ow!

924
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,500
A ray!

925
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:12,290
Yeah, it's a ray all right.

926
00:12:12,290 --> 00:12:15,970
Ray! Ray! You're so amazing, ray!

927
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:20,300
Good luck! Swim! Ray, ray, yeah!

928
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,720
Ray, ray, yeah!

929
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,940
So, the three of you went to the same middle school.

930
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:37,610
Yeah. Was it the winter of second year 
when Izumi moved to Kyushu?

931
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:38,740
I moved to Fukuoka.

932
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,570
Fukuoka <i>is</i> Kyushu.

933
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:47,370
Oh?! What's this?

934
00:12:47,790 --> 00:12:48,960
It's a Japanese bullhead shark!

935
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,370
Japanese bullhead shark?

936
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:55,170
It's also called a Sazaewari.
It eats clams and sea urchin, you know!

937
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:57,260
